#!/usr/bin/python3
"""The layout lint of every Olo app, live: each app with a window opened
in a headless session of its own (a made-up home, demo data where the
app has it, its own D-Bus), every window and every tab of its tab views
reviewed (`{"review":true}` on the app's socket: the checks of
crates/kit-base/src/layout_review.rs) at 1×, 1.5× and 2×, light and dark.
Sound comes from olo-fakesound (a speaker, AirPods and a microphone), so
Preferences ▸ Sound shows its devices, not its empty state.
Errors fail it; review findings (look closely) are listed with --review.

  tools/dev/ui-lint [--dev] [--review] [--keep] [--no-cache] [--jobs N] [--scales 1,1.5,2] [--screen WxH | --screens WxH@S,...] [--tiles [--shots DIR]] [APP...]
  tools/dev/ui-lint --person-screens

--tiles: every window that tiles (not a dialog, an alert, a fixed-size or
floating one) is tiled into each layout in turn, by app_server as a
person's tiling puts it (`Arrange`), and reviewed there, every tab: zoomed,
a vertical half, a horizontal half, a quarter, a vertical third and a
horizontal third (CLAUDE.md, "Every tiling layout"). One whose least size
is bigger than a layout's tile is an error there. Run it on the smallest
screen (`--screen 2560x1600 --scales 2`, 1280 × 800 points) and on the
person's. --shots DIR keeps a picture of each window in each layout and
tab (DIR/APP-LAYOUT[-TAB].png, under DIR/WxH@S/ with --screens), to look
at.

--screens WxH@S,...: each app on each of those screens in turn, each at
its own scale (in place of --screen and --scales), light and dark: what
the pre-push hook runs with --tiles, on the smallest screen and the
person's. --person-screens prints the person's screens so (each one's
size in pixels as it's turned, and its scale), read from their session
(app_server's `outputs`, $OLO_SOCKET: nothing else is asked of it, and
nothing is run there); nothing without a session.

Every app at once, each in a headless session of its own (a copy of the
made-up home, its own sound server), --jobs at a time (a quarter of the
processors by default, four at the most: each session draws on the GPU
the person's desktop draws on, and a dozen at once on a loaded machine
had its jobs time out and the GPU reset under them, 2026-11-20), each
begun only once the machine has room (`wait_for_room`: a quarter of an
hour of waiting at most for the whole run, then on regardless), all at
idle priority (the person's desktop first); the look and scale are changed and the app
asked again until it has drawn them, never waited for longer.

Results are kept (~/.cache/olo-dev/ui-lint.json, one for each app and
way of running it: each screen, scales, --tiles, --review and build
profile its own): an app whose build and
whose lint are as when it last came out clean isn't run again (its
binary's, app_server's and the fake sound server's size, time and inode,
which cargo changes whenever it links them again; this script's,
tsession's and fixture-home's text; the screen, scales and --review). An
app that had errors always runs. --no-cache runs every one.

APP picks some (by name, as listed with --list, or its directory in apps/
as "disk-usage", or "prefs:PANEL"; case and spaces don't count). It
runs release builds: `cargo build --release --workspace` first. Run by
the pre-push hook when UI code changed (tools/hooks), and by
tools/install-session.sh. See "The layout lint" in docs/HACKING.md.

--dev runs the dev profile's builds (target/debug, optimized too) while
you work (CLAUDE.md, "Build what you change"): build the packages you
lint and what the lint runs beside them, `cargo build -p app_server -p
olo-preview -p olo-fakesound -p PACKAGE` (and `-p olo-dnf-fake` for OS
Updates' fake package service), not the whole workspace in release.
"""
import hashlib, json, os, socket, subprocess, sys, threading, time

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
TSESSION = os.path.join(ROOT, "tools/dev/tsession")
BASE = "/var/tmp/olo-dev"
RUNTIME = f"/run/user/{os.getuid()}"
# Which builds it runs: release (the pre-push hook's, and what's ready),
# or with --dev the dev profile's (target/debug), as it's being worked on.
PROFILE = "debug" if "--dev" in sys.argv[1:] else "release"
# Where the builds are: CARGO_TARGET_DIR's, as tsession takes it (a Codex
# subagent builds in a folder of its own, tools/dev/agents), else the
# repository's.
TARGET = os.environ.get("CARGO_TARGET_DIR", os.path.join(ROOT, "target"))

# Preferences' panels (Bluetooth stays out of test runs; AirPods needs
# its fake device).
PANELS = ["ai", "appearance", "backgrounds", "backup", "datetime", "default-apps", "deskbar", "display", "gpus", "integrations", "keyboard", "network", "notifications",
          "performance", "power", "rex", "screensaver", "security", "sound", "terminal", "themes", "touchid", "touchpad", "tracker", "windows", "workspaces", "about"]


